task.statement:
This helper pulls every setting that starts with a prefix and strips the prefix off the key. It builds the dict entry by entry, Java-style, and re-looks-up each value by key.

    def extract_config(settings, prefix):
        config = {}
        for key in settings.keys():
            if key.startswith(prefix):
                value = settings[key]
                config[key[len(prefix):]] = value
        return config

Rewrite it idiomatically in solution.py; same name, same behavior. (Hint: iterate .items() and use a dict comprehension — no empty-dict accumulator, no settings[key] lookup.)

